<title>USA: Health buys three centers, building fourth.</title>
<headline>Health buys three centers, building fourth.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Health Care Property Investors Wednesday said it has bought three assisted-living facilities in Texas for $7.3 million.</p>
<p>The company also said it has committed to fund development of a new $7.4 million, 117-unit, 85,698-square-foot assisted-living facility in Boise, Idaho.</p>
<p>Health Care Property Investors is a self-administered equity-oriented real estate investment trust that invests in health-care facilities.  The company said it has invested in 212 properties either directly or through joint ventures.</p>
</text>
